From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:37:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: Add a driver for the A733 display engine top block

On the A733 the mixer registers read as zero until the reset of their
display is released in the top block of the display engine, and the
route from a display to a TCON is set in that block's DE-to-TCON mux.
sun4i-drm has no driver for it.

Add one in the form of the TCON TOP driver. At probe it enables the
DE bus matrix gate, pulses the DE reset, enables the bus, module and
MBUS clocks, sets bit 16 of the reset and clock registers, registers
the display and MBUS gates as clocks and their resets as a reset
controller, and brings up the MBUS port, which all displays share. It
exports sun60i_de_top_route() for the TCON driver. The providers are
registered at probe time because the mixers take them when they bind,
before this component binds. Routing a display to a TCON disconnects
any other display from that TCON (code 0xf).

Register names, bit positions, bit 16 and the "not connected" code
are vendor values; the vendor sets bit 16 without documenting it. Only
the reset of display 0 is known to be needed on our boards. The DE
reset is pulsed so that no state from the boot chain survives; the
other registers of the page are not written.

Not covered: the DE_SYS bus reset (RST_BUS_DE_SYS), which the vendor
driver also takes. Its reset value is de-asserted, so its state is the
one the boot chain leaves.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the top block released
the clock, reset and MBUS of display 0, routed it to TCON TV1, and the
monitor showed the picture.

Assisted-by: LLM
